  "notes": "The act the lane is named after, written to his own stated design rule — \"I just wanted to be straight-up, and just be simple, [so] people can get what I'm saying 'cause it's a club song.\" That sentence is the model: the kit is an unlayered stock FL Studio 808 kit, the harmony is a pedal plus at most one neighbour, and everything that carries the record is in a 4-to-6-note high-register loop and the hook. So this entry moves AWAY from its parent on the two axes the parent is loose on — `humanize.quantizeStrength` goes up to 0.9 and swing down to 0.52, because this is stock-library grid music rather than the elastic Thug-school pocket the genre model describes. The kick grammar is the research's literal sentence: beat 1 plus a 16th pickup into 3, hence `secondaryAnchor` \"2a\" and a low `syncopation`. ⚠ `modes` is authored here rather than inherited, and it is the whole point of the entry: the research's generator note says **pick the mode first** — Mode A (2007-2010 ringtone snap) is straight-time with the backbeat on 2&4 at 138-142, the swag mode is half-time with the clap on 3 at 136-156, and \"they are different backbeat classes and must never be blended in one generation.\" Authoring modes replaces the genre's swaggy/spacey/slimy set, which is correct: this artist does not do those three, he does these two. ⚠ `confidence` is \"low\" because the research rates him medium-low. What is documented is the era window, the label, the per-single producer credits (Natural Disaster & TopcaT, G5 Kids, Rico Beats, Boi-1da, Bei Maejor, Young Yonny, Inertia), the chart peaks and the intent quote. INFERRED, and marked [LOW-CONF] in the research itself: the exact BPM numbers, the drum placement grammar, the 808 behaviour (`bass808.slideProb` 0.04, `bassline.followRootsProb` 0.96, `glideProb` 0.03 — \"root-only, no glide\"), and the chord numerals. The i-VI and i-VII families are INFERRED from \"chord support rarely exceeds i plus one neighbour\"; the research names no numerals. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set and `maxChords` is 2 because the harmonic content genuinely is the hook, not the pad; the chord part's required variety is carried by `chordDurationBeats` reaching 16 and by three `harmonicRhythm` values, not by progressions this catalogue does not play. ⚠ `snare.layerClapOffsetMs` is [0,1] rather than the parent's [4,10] to spell out \"808 kit, unlayered — single clap/snare on 3\"; the snap-era stack belongs to Mode A's snap lane, not to this one. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts. ⚠ **The 1-bar phrase length was removed** (was [1,2], now [2,4]). A one-bar phrase looped four times carries less entropy than a four-bar phrase, and it is the countermelody it strangles hardest: a counter answers *inside* the melody’s phrase, so a one-bar shape leaves it nowhere to go. Every worst offender on `counter.rs` carried it. ⛔ The previous session recorded this exact mistake and it arrived again from the other direction — distinctness is combinatorial in the shape LENGTH, not in the option count.",
